      "q": "How much does National Aeronautics and Space Administration spend on contracts?",
      "a": "NASA has $10.1B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Obligations are down 36.0% year over year, the agency reported 6,118 awards this fiscal year to date, and the average award size is $1.7M. These totals are partial because current-year figures are fiscal year to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does National Aeronautics and Space Administration buy?",
      "a": "NASA buys research and development, space vehicle manufacturing, engineering, construction, and support services. The top categories in FY2026 to date are Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $4B, Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $1.5B, and Engineering Services at $657M. Other top categories include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Biotechnology) at $605M, Industrial Building Construction at $383M, and Facilities Support Services at $345M."
